(text "Side-link flex — main board J2001 to CM5 board J201" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 20.32 0) (effects (font (size 2.54 2.54) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9b86ff1c-500d-4662-a508-a7a0c5476e31"))
(text "J1 and J2 are the same tail and the flex is the same turned end for end: either tail fits main-board J2001 or\nCM5-board J201, fingers on the contacts, and main-board pin n meets CM5-board pin 25 - n. Main-board pins: 1 GND, 2-3 SIDE_TX_P/N,\n4 GND, 5-6 SIDE_RX_P/N, 7 GND, 8-9 SIDE_D_P/N, 10 GND, 11 CM5_HOST, 12 SIDE_PRESENT_N (grounded on the CM5 board),\n13-14 GND, 15-20 SIDE_BUS, 21-24 GND. Conductors 1, 4, 21 and 24 meet GND at both ends in either fit and join the\nplane; the others stay separate and join on the boards." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 160.02 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9cc8a55e-5177-42d8-ad0c-de7e14103a09"))
(text "Two-layer polyimide flex, 0.19 mm: 50 um core, 18 um copper, coverlay both sides, ENIG fingers. Fingers and\nconductors on B.Cu, every conductor 0.10 mm on the 0.50 mm pitch; GND plane on F.Cu between the finger areas.\nPairs are about 91 Ohm differential over the plane and about 94 Ohm on the fingers. SIDE_BUS takes six conductors,\n0.29 A each at 1.75 A. PI stiffener 0.225 mm on F, 4.2 mm from each tip: 0.34 mm at the fingers against the\nvertical FH12's 0.35 +/-0.03. Fitted bent 180 degrees over the 1.5 mm board gap, about 2.5 mm radius." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 25.4 177.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "34bf4c94-f436-4f2e-a7ab-f4813528d140"))
